ustry using fuel oil as a  source of its power when it is  recognized that we have the highest  concentration of automobiles per square  mile in the world as well as the  nation's third-largest industrial  complex then it must be understood that  the combination of these and our surface  inversions constitute a serious  community problem the Los Angeles County  Air Pollution Control Board headed by  supervisor Warren Dorn has adopted a  policy of requiring controls on every  source of pollution when a reasonable  method for such control exists  the board is holding public hearings on  a rule requiring Los Angeles industry  including their steam power plants to  burn natural gas in preference to fuel  oil during the seven months during which  smog is most likely to occur they are  Pollution Control District is testing  many devices for the control of  pollution from Motor Vehicles in its  automotive combustion laboratory when of  an effective device has been developed  its use will be required on the three  million automobiles operating on our  streets and highways well it's not only  dirt that bothers mrs. public in Los  Angeles and many other cities polluted  air causes physical discomfort too and  we have seen dr. Bernie some of the  functions being performed by the  engineering and medical divisions of the  Public Health Service air pollution  program well it seems to me that the  problem is getting worse rather than  better as you pointed out the more our  society grows the more air is being used  and polluted and the greater are the  demands on the air around us yes and we  have learned that air pollution and smog  are not only unpleasant but may have  definite harmful effects on the health  of the individual there is much to be  done about this growing problem and much  is being done for example in research in  addition to the extensive research  program of the Public Health Service a  great amount of research and analysis is  being conducted in research labor